{:frontmatter
 {:id "adr-2607062300-jk-luxury-org-club-shinshi-net-babiniku-relocation"
  :title "ADR-2607062300: new GitHub org jk-luxury -- relocate club-shinshi and net-babiniku
          out of gftdcojp; crypto-only payment rail for now"
  :status "accepted"
  :doc_type "adr"
  :topic "jk-luxury-org-relocation"
  :authoritative true
  :last_verified "2026-07-06"
  :authoritative_for
  ["club-shinshi and net-babiniku are transferred from gftdcojp to a new jk-luxury GitHub
    org (JK株式会社 legal entity), remaining private, matching a pre-existing informal
    entity split already on record"
   "manifest/repos.edn gains a jk-luxury :orgs entry (:role :human-centric :scope :business)
    and two :path-overrides entries (gftdcojp/{club-shinshi,net-babiniku} ->
    jk-luxury/{club-shinshi,net-babiniku}), following the same precedent as every prior
    GitHub-org transfer in this repo"
   "ADR-2607062200's payment-rail decision is amended: crypto-only for now (not fiat/adult
    PSP) -- but the vendor/etzhayyim centralization-axis boundary (ADR-2605211950,
    ADR-2605172100) is UNCHANGED and still binding: self-custody on-chain settlement code
    still may not be scaffolded in net-babiniku itself, regardless of which org it now lives
    in"]
  :related
  ["90-docs/adr/2607062200-net-babiniku-onlyfans-style-creator-monetization.md"
   "90-docs/adr/2607062210-net-babiniku-giemon-humanoid-embodiment-procurement.md"
   "orgs/etzhayyim/root/90-docs/adr/2605211950-vendor-centralized-etzhayyim-decentralized-substrate-axis.md"
   "orgs/etzhayyim/root/90-docs/adr/2605172100-etzhayyim-payments-on-chain-only.md"]
  :supersedes []
  :superseded_by []}

 :problem
 {:source "user direction 2026-07-06: created https://github.com/jk-luxury, directed that
           club-shinshi and net-babiniku be relocated there, private; separately, directed
           crypto-only payment rail for now (narrower than ADR-2607062200's fiat-primary
           decision)"
  :pre_existing_split "gftd-talent-actor docs already note 'itonami (Gftd Japan株式会社,
                       cloud-itonami) serves club-shinshi (JK株式会社)' -- club-shinshi was
                       already operated under a different legal entity than the rest of
                       gftdcojp, even though its repo lived under the gftdcojp GitHub org"
  :why_now "both club-shinshi and net-babiniku are adult-content-adjacent creator-economy
            products (ADR-2607062200, ADR-2607062210 land in the same session); giving them
            their own org boundary scopes any future PSP/compliance audit surface cleanly,
            separate from gftdcojp's other business lines"
  :risk_check
  {:club_shinshi "private, no .github/workflows/, no webhooks -- deploys are manual CLI"
   :net_babiniku "private, no .github/workflows/, no webhooks -- deploys via `wrangler pages
                  deploy`, no custom domain bound (net-babiniku.pages.dev)"
   :conclusion "no GitHub-App-triggered CI/CD exists for either repo, so an org transfer
               carries materially lower operational risk than it would for a repo with
               org-scoped Actions secrets or a GitHub-App-linked deploy pipeline"}}

 :decision
 {:new_org
  {:name "jk-luxury"
   :repos_edn_orgs_entry {:role :human-centric :scope :business}
   :rationale "GitHub home for the JK株式会社 legal entity, carved out of gftdcojp (Gftd Japan
              株式会社) for adult-content/creator-economy products, matching the pre-existing
              informal entity split"}
  :transfer
  {:what "club-shinshi and net-babiniku transferred gftdcojp -> jk-luxury via
          gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/transfer, remaining private"
   :local_checkouts "orgs/gftdcojp/{club-shinshi,net-babiniku} moved to
                     orgs/jk-luxury/{club-shinshi,net-babiniku}, matching the established
                     path-override precedent for every prior GitHub-org transfer in this repo
                     (manimani->gftdcojp, cloud-manimani->gftdcojp,
                     cloud-murakumo->local-murakumo, kototama->kotoba-lang)"}
  :repos_edn_path_overrides
  ["orgs/gftdcojp/club-shinshi -> orgs/jk-luxury/club-shinshi"
   "orgs/gftdcojp/net-babiniku -> orgs/jk-luxury/net-babiniku"]
  :extra_projects_entry_unchanged "net-babiniku's original :extra-projects entry (registered
                                   under ADR-2607051800) is left textually unchanged -- the
                                   override is the record of the subsequent move, not a
                                   rewrite of history"
  :west_yml_regeneration "bb scripts/gen-west-manifest.bb --entry club-shinshi --entry
                          net-babiniku -- minimal-diff, not a wholesale regeneration, per
                          ADR-2607022900"
  :payment_rail_amendment
  {:what "net-babiniku's monetization launches with ONLY the crypto/USDC rail, not the
          fiat/adult-PSP rail ADR-2607062200 specified as primary"
   :boundary_unchanged "self-custody on-chain settlement code still may not be scaffolded in
                       net-babiniku itself -- the vendor/etzhayyim centralization-axis
                       boundary (ADR-2605211950, ADR-2605172100) was never gftdcojp-specific,
                       it applies to any vendor-side repo, jk-luxury included. Actual
                       settlement logic must still live in etzhayyim/root, consumed via a
                       consent-capability boundary; net-babiniku implements only the domain
                       model/governor/ledger/UI that call into that capability"
   :chain_custody_undecided "concrete chain/wallet-custody choice is NOT decided by this ADR
                             -- building real fund-moving code without that input would be
                             premature; this round's implementation stubs the actual
                             settlement call behind the same honest-default/no-fake-checkout
                             pattern ADR-2607062200 already established for the fiat rail"}}

 :consequences
 {:org_scoped_governance "club-shinshi and net-babiniku now governed by jk-luxury's (JK
                          株式会社's) access control/billing surface, separate from
                          gftdcojp's -- future PSP/compliance audit scopes cleanly to one org"
  :historical_path_references "cross-references to the old gftdcojp/{club-shinshi,
                               net-babiniku} paths elsewhere (ADR-2607062200,
                               ADR-2607062210, gftd-talent-actor docs) become historical --
                               GitHub's transfer redirect keeps old remote URLs working;
                               those documents are not retroactively rewritten"
  :no_ci_breakage_expected "neither repo had CI/webhooks pre-transfer; any FUTURE
                           GitHub-App-based integration will need re-authorization for
                           jk-luxury specifically"
  :fiat_deferred_not_cancelled "ADR-2607062200's original fiat/adult-PSP rail remains the
                                eventual second rail once a PSP is actually contracted"
  :chain_selection_followup "concrete crypto chain/custody-provider selection remains a
                            business/security decision this ADR does not make; real
                            fund-moving code is not implemented until that's resolved"}

 :alternatives
 [{:option "keep both repos under gftdcojp, rely on repo-level access control only"
   :rejected_because "the org itself is the natural boundary for an already-distinct legal
                      entity (JK株式会社); the informal split was already on record, this
                      just makes the GitHub structure match it"}
  {:option "create fresh repos under jk-luxury with clean history instead of transferring"
   :rejected_because "a GitHub transfer preserves issues/stars/history and both repos are
                      recent/small with no CI coupling to lose; a clean-history split made
                      sense for club-shinshi's original monorepo extraction but is
                      unnecessary overhead for an org-only move of already-standalone repos"}
  {:option "silently rewrite the existing :extra-projects entry's path instead of adding a
            :path-overrides entry"
   :rejected_because "every prior GitHub-org transfer in this repo used :path-overrides with
                      a dated rationale comment, preserving the original registration
                      decision's text; breaking that convention here would lose the audit
                      trail this repo otherwise maintains carefully"}]}
